## Driving to the spa town: what to know about parking first

Marienbad is compact and wonderfully walkable — but that doesn’t mean you can’t arrive by car. Quite the opposite. Most visitors come by car, and the key question is: **where to park?** The historic centre sits inside a protected [spa zone](/en/colonnade) with restricted access, so it pays to plan your parking before you arrive.

The good news: most [Ensana hotels](/en/accommodation) offer their own parking, and the town also has several parking houses and public car parks. This guide covers the essentials; **for the full overview of prices and capacity at each hotel, see the [Parking at the Ensana Hotels](/en/parking) page**.

## Parking at the Ensana hotels

At the hotels you’ll usually find three kinds of spaces:

- **Unguarded car park in front of the hotel** — free at some hotels, but with a limited number of spaces.
- **Guarded car park** — the safer option, typically 250–380 CZK per day (the price drops for longer stays).
- **Underground garages** — at the Nové Lázně and Hvězda resorts, monitored and sheltered from the weather.

One exception is the **Pacifik**: the spaces right by the hotel are for check-in and check-out only; for the length of your stay you’ll use the nearby parking house by the Municipal Theatre.

For **all** hotel car parks and garages, one rule applies: **advance reservation is required**. Capacity is limited and in season spaces fill up quickly, so secure yours when you book your stay — simply email the hotel (e.g. *res.nl@ensanahotels.com* for Nové Lázně). You’ll find specific prices, space counts and contacts for each hotel in the [overview table](/en/parking).

## Electric, hybrid and LPG cars

An important note for owners of alternative-fuel vehicles: the **underground garages** at the Hvězda and Butterfly hotels **do not allow electric, hybrid or LPG vehicles**. If you arrive in such a car, use the hotel’s outdoor car park or one of the town car parks below.

## Parking around town

When hotel spaces are full — or you need to park away from the hotel — the town offers several options:

- **Parking Centrum (parking house)**, Pramenská 653/2 behind the Municipal Theatre. Covered, guarded, with CCTV, open around the clock, 290 spaces. First 20 minutes free, 20 CZK/hour, 240 CZK/day. This is the “parking house by the Municipal Theatre” within walking distance of the Pacifik, Butterfly and Svoboda hotels.
- **Central car park**, Kollárova 94/26 — guarded, with a ticket machine, around the clock, 400 spaces, 50 CZK/day.
- **Public car parks with a ticket machine** by the Koliba and Krakonoš hotels or by Oděvy — cheaper options for shorter stays.

## The spa zone: entry by permit only

The heart of town — the colonnade, the Singing Fountain and the spa houses — lies within the **spa zone**, where access is regulated. Guests staying inside the zone are exempt on their arrival and departure days. Otherwise you need a permit: a **one-day spa-zone permit** can be bought from a parking machine for 20 CZK.

There are more than 30 parking meters around the centre; hourly rates run from roughly 30 to 50 CZK depending on the zone (highest in the spa centre).

## How to pay

The machines accept **payment cards** and the **ClickPark** mobile app, which also tracks the end of your parking time. **Cash payment** (CZK and €) is only possible at certain new-type machines that are still being rolled out across town — so don’t rely on coins alone. The town also has interactive boards showing the number of free spaces at each location.

## Summary and links

- At the hotel, **always reserve parking in advance**, ideally when you book your stay.
- Electric, hybrid or LPG? **Not in the underground garages** — use outdoor or town car parks.
- The spa zone requires a **permit** (or accommodation inside the zone).
- Pay by card or **ClickPark**; cash only at the new machines.

For the detailed overview of parking at each hotel — with prices, capacity and contacts — see the [**Parking at the Ensana Hotels**](/en/parking) page. Still choosing a hotel? Take a look at [accommodation in Marienbad](/en/accommodation).
